    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Scales from top to bottom: $\\pm1$, $\\pm2.5$, $\\pm0.5$, $\\pm0.25$, $\\pm0.125$, $\\pm0.05$.",
      "worked": "Absolute error is half the scale increment. For the scales from top to bottom:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Absolute error}_1 &= \\tfrac12\\times2=1\\\\\\text{Absolute error}_2 &= \\tfrac12\\times5=2.5\\\\\\text{Absolute error}_3 &= \\tfrac12\\times1=0.5\\\\\\text{Absolute error}_4 &= \\tfrac12\\times0.5=0.25\\\\\\text{Absolute error}_5 &= \\tfrac12\\times0.25=0.125\\\\\\text{Absolute error}_6 &= \\tfrac12\\times0.1=0.05\\end{aligned}$$\nMatch these to $\\pm1$, $\\pm2.5$, $\\pm0.5$, $\\pm0.25$, $\\pm0.125$ and $\\pm0.05$, respectively.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
